  WARN  [misplacement-ledger] layers/core-ui/src/fixtures/knowledge-data.ts: production path, really development — Mock knowledge items in a production path, imported by the shipping `KnowledgeDetail` page as the fallback when the API returns nothing. Moving the file into a `__` folder would turn a production page into an importer of a development file, which the crossing rule forbids outright — so the fixture cannot move until the page stops needing it. The fix is the API, not a relocation.
  WARN  [misplacement-ledger] layers/core-ui/src/pages/_dev/ArtifactDemo.tsx: production path, really development — A development-only preview page sitting in a production path. `_dev` is one underscore, so the folder clause (`__`) does not claim it, and renaming the folder is not a free fix: `router.tsx` would then be a production file importing a development one. It clears when the artifact surfaces it previews land as real routes and this page is deleted.
  WARN  [misplacement-ledger] layers/core-ui/src/router.tsx: production path, really development — Production, and correctly so — but it registers the `/_dev/artifacts` route behind `import.meta.env.DEV`, and that registration is the only thing keeping the development-only preview page reachable. Recorded here as well as the page because deleting the route is the act that clears the page. Two specs under `layers/core-ui/__e2e__/` navigate to it, so it cannot be dropped before they have a real surface to drive.

